摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Noema long-term memory plugin for DSH: durable, inspectable agent memory with recall tools and a settings page.","id":"gh:1334167430","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-noema","slug":"ZSeven-W/dsh-noema","topics":["agent-memory","ai-agents","coding-agent","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","long-term-memory","mcp","memory","noema","plugin","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Noema long-term memory plugin for DSH: durable, inspectable agent memory with recall tools and a set"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"term memory plugin for DSH: durable, inspectable agent memory with recall tools and a settings page."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"DSH Noema"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Long-term memory for DeepSeek Harness — durable, inspectable agent memory backed by Noema."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Recall Before Work • Import From 9 Agent Tools • Settings-Page Memory Management • Crash Keep-Alive "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"e Work • Import From 9 Agent Tools • Settings-Page Memory Management • Crash Keep-Alive • Hot Reload"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"npm: @zseven-w/dsh-noema · Tested with DSH 0.2.0-rc.2"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"English · 简体中文 · 繁體中文 · 日本語 · 한국어 · Français · Español · Deutsch · Português · Русский · हिन्दी · Tü"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"rkçe · ไทย · Tiếng Việt · Bahasa Indonesia"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"The Noema Memory settings page — import sources, memory management, and live server status"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Why DSH Noema"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"DSH Noema connects DeepSeek Harness with Noema — a local-first, non-vector memory system for coding "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"agents — so an Agent keeps durable knowledge across sessions instead of starting every conversation "},{"id":"p9s3","text":"o an Agent keeps durable knowledge across sessions instead of starting every conversation from zero."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### 🧠 Durable Recall"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Memories persist as inspectable Markdown files under `NOEMA_ROOT` (default `~/.agent-memory/`). `noe"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ma_recall` loads relevant context at the start of a session; `noema_search`, `noema_browse`, `noema_"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"catalog`, and `noema_recall_graph` cover lookup, exploration, and auditing."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### 📥 Import From Other Tools"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"`noema_import` reads the memory files of ten other AI coding tools — Codex, Claude Code, opencode, C"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ursor, Grok, WorkBuddy, Antigravity, Trae, Qoder, Hermes — splits them into sections, and saves each"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" as a durable memory. A content-keyed ledger deduplicates across runs and across tools that share fi"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"a durable memory. A content-keyed ledger deduplicates across runs and across tools that share files."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### 🛠️ Settings-Page Management"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The Noema Memory settings page configures the server command, memory root, budgets, idle/call timeou"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ts, and the guidance section — and a Manage memories card searches, browses, adds, reviews, and dele"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"tes stored memories directly."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### 🩺 Keep-Alive"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The memory server stays up: idle timeout defaults to never, and a keep-alive loop restarts the `noem"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"a-mcp` child in the background when it crashes or exits, with a configurable check interval and rest"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" in the background when it crashes or exits, with a configurable check interval and restart backoff."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### 🔍 Smart Entity Extraction"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Noema's extraction engine combines jieba word segmentation with high-precision signals — English pro"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"per nouns, CJK names and technical terms, quoted topics, and repetition — with stopword and path fil"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"ters, so the PageIndex topic catalog stays clean."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### ⚡ Hot Reload"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"After the first boot, the plugin never needs a restart again: `pnpm run build` hot-reloads the host "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"plugin through Cordis HMR, and `ppnpm run build:client` hot-swaps the browser bundle over the client"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"rdis HMR, and `ppnpm run build:client` hot-swaps the browser bundle over the client-hmr SSE channel."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Install into DSH"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Or, for local development straight from the source tree:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The `link:` protocol symlinks the profile dependency to this repository, so rebuilds are visible imm"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"ediately and Cordis HMR can watch the compiled output."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The plugin bundles the `noema-mcp` binary through per-platform optional npm packages. To build it yo"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"urself instead, run `cargo build --release -p noema-mcp` inside the bundled `noema` submodule, or po"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"int the Server command setting at any `noema-mcp` build."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Memory Tools"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The model-facing tools mirror the Noema MCP surface:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Tool | What it does |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| `noema_recall` | Recall relevant memories for a query, with a token budget. |\n| `noema_search` | F"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"ull-text search over stored memories. |\n| `noema_browse` | Browse the PageIndex catalog for a topic "},{"id":"p31s3","text":"or entity. |\n| `noema_catalog` | Render the full memory catalog as markdown. |\n| `noema_recall_graph"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"` | Multi-hop recall through links and shared entities. |\n| `noema_neighbors` | One graph hop from a"},{"id":"p31s5","text":" memory. |\n| `noema_explain` | Explain why a memory was or was not recalled. |\n| `noema_remember` | "},{"id":"p31s6","text":"Save a durable fact, decision, constraint, or preference. |\n| `noema_review_list` | List pending rev"},{"id":"p31s7","text":"iew candidates. |\n| `noema_review_decide` | Accept, reject, edit, or merge a candidate. |\n| `noema_f"},{"id":"p31s8","text":"orget` | Tombstone or hard-delete a memory. |\n| `noema_policy_get` / `noema_policy_set` | Read or up"},{"id":"p31s9","text":"date the write policy. |\n| `noema_status` | Server and tenant status: counts, index health, storage "},{"id":"p31s10","text":"root. |\n| `noema_import` | Import memories from other AI coding tools. |"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Each tool returns a uniform envelope `{ ok, tool, text }` where `text` carries the full server outpu"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"ch tool returns a uniform envelope `{ ok, tool, text }` where `text` carries the full server output."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Import memories from other tools"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"| Source id | Global files | Workspace files |"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| `codex` | `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` + the Codex memory pipeline: `~/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md`, `memory"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"_summary.md`, `rollout_summaries/*.md`, `extensions/ad_hoc/notes/*.md` (`raw_memories.md` skipped — "},{"id":"p35s3","text":"it is the uncurated feed) | `AGENTS.md`, `AGENTS.local.md` |\n| `claude-code` | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`"},{"id":"p35s4","text":", `~/.claude/CLAUDE.local.md`, `~/.claude/MEMORY.md` | `CLAUDE.md`, `CLAUDE.local.md`, `MEMORY.md` |"},{"id":"p35s5","text":"\n| `opencode` | `~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md` | `AGENTS.md` |\n| `cursor` | `~/.cursor/rules/*.mdc`,"},{"id":"p35s6","text":" `~/.cursorrules` | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, `.cursorrules` |\n| `grok` | `~/.grok/AGENTS.md` + the Gro"},{"id":"p35s7","text":"k cross-session memory: `~/.grok/memory/MEMORY.md`, per-project `MEMORY.md`, and `sessions/*.md` sum"},{"id":"p35s8","text":"maries | `AGENTS.md` |\n| `workbuddy` | `~/.codebuddy/CODEBUDDY.md` (WorkBuddy memory file), `~/.work"},{"id":"p35s9","text":"buddy/AGENTS.md`, `~/.workbuddy/memory.md`, `~/.config/workbuddy/AGENTS.md`, `~/Library/Application "},{"id":"p35s10","text":"Support/WorkBuddy/AGENTS.md` | `AGENTS.md`, `CODEBUDDY.md` |\n| `antigravity` | `~/.antigravity/AGENT"},{"id":"p35s11","text":"S.md`, `~/.config/antigravity/AGENTS.md`, `~/Library/Application Support/Antigravity/AGENTS.md` (bes"},{"id":"p35s12","text":"t-effort; no documented global memory store yet) | `AGENTS.md`, `AGENTS.local.md` |\n| `trae` | `~/.t"},{"id":"p35s13","text":"rae/AGENTS.md`, `~/.trae/memory/`, `~/.trae/rules/` (plus the `~/.trae-cn` variants) | `AGENTS.md`, "},{"id":"p35s14","text":"`.trae/rules/` |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
